# Angular Migration Guide

**Step-by-step guide for migrating Angular applications to latest versions**

## Pre-Migration Checklist

### 1. Check Current Version
```bash
ng version
```

### 2. Review Breaking Changes
- Check [Angular Update Guide](https://update.angular.io/)
- Review changelog for target version
- Identify deprecated APIs

### 3. Update Dependencies
```bash
# Check for outdated packages
npm outdated

# Update Angular CLI
npm install -g @angular/cli@latest
```

## Migration Process

### Step 1: Update Angular CLI
```bash
# Update globally
npm install -g @angular/cli@latest

# Update in project
ng update @angular/cli
```

### Step 2: Update Core Packages
```bash
# Update Angular core packages
ng update @angular/core @angular/cli

# Update with automatic migrations
ng update @angular/core @angular/cli --migrate-only
```

### Step 3: Update Other Packages
```bash
# Update Angular Material
ng update @angular/material

# Update other Angular packages
ng update @angular/cdk
ng update @angular/router
```

## Common Migrations

### Migrating to Standalone Components

#### Before (NgModule)
```typescript
// app.module.ts
@NgModule({
  declarations: [UserComponent],
  imports: [CommonModule, FormsModule],
  providers: [UserService]
})
export class AppModule {}

// user.component.ts
@Component({
  selector: 'app-user',
  template: `...`
})
export class UserComponent {}
```

#### After (Standalone)
```typescript
// user.component.ts
@Component({
  selector: 'app-user',
  standalone: true,
  imports: [CommonModule, FormsModule],
  template: `...`
})
export class UserComponent {}

// main.ts
bootstrapApplication(AppComponent, {
  providers: [UserService]
});
```

### Migrating to Signals

#### Before (RxJS)
```typescript
export class UserService {
  private users$ = new BehaviorSubject<User[]>([]);
  
  getUsers() {
    return this.users$.asObservable();
  }
  
  loadUsers() {
    this.http.get<User[]>('/api/users')
      .subscribe(users => this.users$.next(users));
  }
}
```

#### After (Signals)
```typescript
import { signal, computed } from '@angular/core';

export class UserService {
  private users = signal<User[]>([]);
  readonly users$ = this.users.asReadonly();
  
  userCount = computed(() => this.users().length);
  
  loadUsers() {
    this.http.get<User[]>('/api/users')
      .subscribe(users => this.users.set(users));
  }
}
```

### Migrating to New Control Flow

#### Before (Structural Directives)
```html
<div *ngIf="user">
  <p>{{ user.name }}</p>
</div>

<div *ngFor="let item of items">
  {{ item.name }}
</div>

<div [ngSwitch]="status">
  <p *ngSwitchCase="'active'">Active</p>
  <p *ngSwitchDefault>Inactive</p>
</div>
```

#### After (New Control Flow)
```html
@if (user()) {
  <p>{{ user().name }}</p>
}

@for (item of items(); track item.id) {
  <div>{{ item.name }}</div>
}

@switch (status()) {
  @case ('active') {
    <p>Active</p>
  }
  @default {
    <p>Inactive</p>
  }
}
```

### Migrating HTTP Client

#### Before (HttpClient with RxJS)
```typescript
export class UserService {
  users$ = this.http.get<User[]>('/api/users').pipe(
    shareReplay(1)
  );
}
```

#### After (Signals with toSignal)
```typescript
import { toSignal } from '@angular/core/rxjs-interop';

export class UserService {
  users = toSignal(
    this.http.get<User[]>('/api/users'),
    { initialValue: [] }
  );
}
```

